  + [text] is "I don't know what to do from here, but I imagine this system should run like a neural net I/O for semantic coordination, and as such, it operates like a lens to focus identity and meaning for intended purposes that can be re-entered when the associations in the semantic neural net co-processor have a high coherence... would the inference engine have to load these purposes and attention bindings into some hash system? but the SOP framework is like a 255-dimension forest of meaning that the agent needs to navigate. pants decomposition of the hyperbolic plane... I don't know if my visual intuition helps, but I imagined a navigation instrument in attention that brings out the associations of an element in focus on a kind of ball-graph where you see the surface from one focal point and it divides out on the pants relationship graph, and you can peek into/around elements that pass through the focus of attention? intelligence is in the pattern which is employed to search this space of \"degrees of separation from direct associations\" (is that a fair description? degrees of separation)"

